From e053d3494147e2a68e9bcaaf002a491933101f22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:23:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban consent/delivery: scope claim negation to the
 verb; fail closed on unsynced provenance

Follow-up to PR #1783 review (5885372987) non-blocking points:

1. claimed_targets: a negation/intent word only undoes a delivery claim when it
   governs the verb (up to 3 words before it, stopping at a comma or
   conjunction). "Delivered the note to t_X with no errors" now needs the exact
   receipt; "not posted", "queued, not yet posted", "failed and was not sent"
   stay outside the gate. Read-only replay over 339 local done summaries: the
   only change is one real claim the old rule missed.
2. Home executor: a caller whose created event has not reached the replica is
   retried (like an unreachable Board) and refused as consent_unproven after
   CREATION_SYNC_GRACE_S, never applied on an empty read.
3. _submit also enforces the submitting session's own stops, and cards created
   by a session inherit that session's stops even when they carry the parent's
   origin-chat session_id. The remaining limit (home cannot see a submitting
   host's session stops; later stops do not reach existing cards) is documented
   in kanban_consent.
4. The snapshot fallback reads the request-scoped session
   (get_session_env('HERMES_SESSION_ID')), not os.environ.
---
